͸, which Э proper stems and č. After these
come the ͹, or flowerless plants, such as the ferns which
possess stems and č. Farther up are the flowering plants,
then the Å trees, and then what are known
as our "forest trees" and fruit-bearing trees.
Nature never क. She works in a ͺ „, ex-
perimenting continuously. The same natural transition can
be seen in Æ.
